@tradition reading-corner
// Reading corner (0.60.7, the user's pick): on Sunday afternoons crew bring a book to the bow lounge armchairs and read
// together quietly, with a few murmured recommendations.
k: 452
title: Reading corner
when: weekly sunday
at: 16:00-17:00
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: quiet-corner 60%, window-seat 35%, lounge-regular 30%, everyone 10%
anim: read
from: The bow lounge


== mail
- Reading corner on Sunday at {time} in the bow lounge. Bring a book, or borrow one. Quiet voices, comfy chairs.

== ask
- Reading corner this afternoon. Bring a book. Or just sit.
- Quiet hour in the lounge armchairs later. Come and read.

== here
- Shh. Good bit. Very good bit.   #funny
- You'd like this one. Borrow it after.
- Best armchair's by the window. Quick.

== thanks
- You settle into a lounge armchair with a book. Pages turn, someone murmurs a recommendation, and the afternoon slows down.   #warm

== chatter
- Reading corner Sunday. Best armchair is mine.   #funny
- Got a book recommendation from reading corner. Loved it.
- Quietest hour on the ship, reading corner.
